>>__ Parse.temp_set_grammars $ valOf $ grammarDB {thyname="hol"};
## `mk_simpset`

``` hol4
simpLib.mk_simpset : ssfrag list -> simpset
```

------------------------------------------------------------------------

Creates a simpset by combining a list of `ssfrag` values.

This function creates a `simpset` value by repeatedly adding (as per the
`++` operator) `simpset` fragment values to the base `empty_ss`.
Fragments may carry strategy settings (loopers, solvers and split rules,
made with `simpLib.looper_ss`, `simpLib.solver_ss`, `simpLib.safe_solver_ss`
and `simpLib.split_ss`) as well as rewrites, so these too are added in order.

`simpLib.ssfrags_of ss` gives only the fragments of `ss`: a simpset
rebuilt from them loses the deletions, exclusions, limit and settings of
`ss`.

### Failure

Never fails.

Creates simpsets, which are a necessary argument to any simplification
function.

